Bill, my neutral gnomish female wizard (I just decided to give her a 
man's name) was doing rather well. A bones file in the mines comprising 
several bodies fitted her out with some nice stash, included a +3 small 
shield from a valkyrie ;-) . Picked up the amulet in Sokoban, several 
bags of holding on the floor and a very useful ring of conflict. She 
sacrificed for Magicbane early on, and then murdered most of minetown to 
get the priests robe - I didn't realise that angering someone else's god 
loses telepathy telepathy.

Lacking any levitating methods, she dug down from medusa, found a 
co-aligned temple just above the castle (this would have been a really 
useful stash!) Found a handy level teleport to get back to lvl 7 and 
stock up, then proceeded to the castle...

Thinking she was being very clever, she filled in the moat (only 
port-humously remembering the cone of cold she'd recently learned) and 
smashed the drawbridge with force bolt. While standing in front of it.
You die.

Bugger, by far the most successful wizard I'v ever played.
How far away do you have to be from a drawbridge to be safe when blowing 
it apart?

We all learn the hard way...


